Subject: Cantor Resumable Coordination Tool P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 9cc52fe8-2d8b-4b1a-b250-b9783b6bbaaf
@ [canonical] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Resumable_Coordination_Tool_P0.sop

& [Need] is an ordinary callable seam
  + the checkpoint stepper proves execution-frame reentry but is currently reachable only by Rust callers
  + the requested inference coprocessor requires strict machine forms a transport-neutral dispatcher and a standard local tool surface
  + a later model pass must be able to inspect the complete response rather than trust an operator paraphrase

& [Leverage] is unusually high for a thin adapter
  + one command makes the proven deterministic runtime callable by Codex llama.cpp or any MCP-capable host without modifying inference engines
  + stateless requests make all authority visible and make crash recovery identical to resubmission
  + isolating MCP preserves a reusable Rust dispatcher for other transports

& [Safety] follows the checkpoint core
  + every call carries the exact admitted context and the core rechecks lineage
  + no server-held memory can silently diverge between callers
  + finite input size closed forms and typed failures bound the parsing and execution surface

& [Tradeoff] accepts larger repeated requests
  + the six static context objects repeat on every P0 advance call
  + this is intentional until measurements justify a separately governed context registry
  + correctness inspectability and restart simplicity take priority over premature transport compression

& [AlternativesRejected] prevents duplicated authority
  - modifying llama.cpp first would tie the semantic proof to one host
  - a stateful MCP first would add custody recovery and concurrency obligations
  - extending the old procedure command would confuse full authorship orchestration with bounded checkpoint stepping

& [Conclusion] is implement one strict pure dispatcher and one stateless local STDIO MCP adapter

